// cmd/sim_runner/main.go — Generated by CIaC (v0.24 M9, full parity
// 27UpdatePlan.md M7).
//
// Scenario-driving simulation runner. Interprets the same closed
// request/publish/advance/drain/expect scenario vocabulary ciac-sim's
// Scenario JSON schema defines, against this service's own generated
// routes.Router (through net/http/httptest, no live listener) and its
// worker HandleMessageOnce.../job HandleTickOnce... entry points --
// line-for-line the same architecture as sim_runner.rs.j2/
// sim_runner.ts.j2, generated (not a shared library) because this
// needs concrete per-program types, exactly like the Rust/TypeScript
// backends' own generated runners. Included in `go build ./...`/
// `go vet ./...`/`go test ./...` automatically (a second `main`
// package under its own directory, the same way Cargo auto-discovers
// `src/bin/sim_runner.rs`), so no `TargetInfo.validate` change was
// needed to pick it up.
//
// Single-service only; `publish` steps (publishing directly to a
// stream, bypassing an API) are not wired -- the same disclosed scope
// Rust's/TypeScript's own runners still carry. Any scenario step this
// runner cannot honor is a hard error, never a silently-skipped no-op.
// Structural scenario parsing only (simulation_version/non-empty
// steps) -- this is a hand-written restatement of
// ciac_sim::scenario::Scenario, not that vendored Rust source, the
// same position Python's/TypeScript's own hand-written scenario
// drivers occupy.
package main

import (
	"bytes"
	"encoding/base64"
	"encoding/json"
	"errors"
	"fmt"
	"net/http"
